<title>MACEDONIA: MACEDONIA INFLATION SLOWS IN FEBRUARY TO -0.4.</title>
<headline>MACEDONIA INFLATION SLOWS IN FEBRUARY TO -0.4.</headline>
<dateline>SKOPJE 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Macedonia's monthly consumer price inflation slowed in February to -0.4 percent from 3.9 percent in January, the National Bank of Macedonia said.</p>
<p>Inflation in January rose after the government hiked post and telephone charges and transport prices, said an NBM official.</p>
<p>A tight monetary policy sustained by the government over the past several years has sharply brought annual inflation down from 2,000 percent in 1993 to three percent in 1996.</p>
<p> MACEDONIA CONSUMER PRICES   (FEB)    (JAN)	 (FEB 1996)</p>
<p> monthly pct change	     -0.4    +3.9	    0 </p>
<p> year-on-year		     +3.3    +3.7	    5.5</p>
<p>-- Elisaveta Konstantinova, Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
